<title>ITALY: Italy's Rinascente suspended on bourse.</title>
<headline>Italy's Rinascente suspended on bourse.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Italian retailer Rinascente have been suspended on the Milan stock market for today in expectation of an announcement, bourse watchdog Consob said.</p>
<p>Rinascente shares closed on Monday at 9358 lire per share.</p>
<p>The company, Italy's largest quoted retail group, is controlled by the Agnelli family holding company IFIL.</p>
<p>--Milan bureau +39 2 66129507</p>
</text>
